  "sermonTitle": "Vision Isn't Enough",
  "speaker": null,
  "sermonScripture": null,
  "topScriptures": [],
  "introduction": "These questions are designed to help Crews discuss the weekend teaching while building relationships with each other and applying God's Word to our lives.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "sec-warm-up",
      "title": "WARM UP",
      "order": 1,
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "q-warm-up-1",
          "order": 1,
          "segments": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "What's one moment from this summer that you're especially grateful for?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "q-warm-up-2",
          "order": 2,
          "segments": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Describe your summer using three words."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "q-warm-up-3",
          "order": 3,
          "segments": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Looking back at your notes from this week's teaching, was there anything that particularly caught your attention, challenged you, or confused you?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sec-know-it",
      "title": "KNOW IT",
      "order": 2,
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "q-know-it-1",
          "order": 1,
          "segments": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Christian life is a continual journey of becoming more like Jesus. As we grow, we align our lives with God's heart and purposes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "q-know-it-2",
          "order": 2,
          "segments": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "What does alignment with God mean to you? What are you currently aiming your life toward, and how has that \"bullseye\" shifted over time?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "q-know-it-3",
          "order": 3,
          "segments": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Read: "
            },
            {
              "type": "scripture",
              "displayText": "Colossians 3:23",
              "reference": {
                "book": "Colossians",
                "bookId": "COL",
                "chapter": 3,
                "verseStart": 23
              },
              "references": [
                {
                  "book": "Colossians",
                  "bookId": "COL",
                  "chapter": 3,
                  "verseStart": 23
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", "
            },
            {
              "type": "scripture",
              "displayText": "1 Corinthians 10:31",
              "reference": {
                "book": "1 Corinthians",
                "bookId": "1CO",
                "chapter": 10,
                "verseStart": 31
              },
              "references": [
                {
                  "book": "1 Corinthians",
                  "bookId": "1CO",
                  "chapter": 10,
                  "verseStart": 31
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", "
            },
            {
              "type": "scripture",
              "displayText": "Psalm 37:5",
              "reference": {
                "book": "Psalms",
                "bookId": "PSA",
                "chapter": 37,
                "verseStart": 5
              },
              "references": [
                {
                  "book": "Psalms",
                  "bookId": "PSA",
                  "chapter": 37,
                  "verseStart": 5
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", "
            },
            {
              "type": "scripture",
              "displayText": "Proverbs 16:3",
              "reference": {
                "book": "Proverbs",
                "bookId": "PRO",
                "chapter": 16,
                "verseStart": 3
              },
              "references": [
                {
                  "book": "Proverbs",
                  "bookId": "PRO",
                  "chapter": 16,
                  "verseStart": 3
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "q-know-it-4",
          "order": 4,
          "segments": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Following Jesus is personal, but it was never meant to be lived alone. When the church is aligned around Jesus and His purposes, something begins to overflow into the way we live."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "q-know-it-5",
          "order": 5,
          "segments": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "When a church is truly aligned together around Jesus, what do you think naturally overflows from that community?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "q-know-it-6",
          "order": 6,
          "segments": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Read: "
            },
            {
              "type": "scripture",
              "displayText": "Acts 2:42-47",
              "reference": {
                "book": "Acts",
                "bookId": "ACT",
                "chapter": 2,
                "verseStart": 42,
                "verseEnd": 47
              },
              "references": [
                {
                  "book": "Acts",
