        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sec-share-it",
      "title": "SHARE IT",
      "order": 3,
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "q-share-it-1",
          "order": 1,
          "segments": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Read: "
            },
            {
              "type": "scripture",
              "displayText": "Colossians 3:1-4",
              "reference": {
                "book": "Colossians",
                "bookId": "COL",
                "chapter": 3,
                "verseStart": 1,
                "verseEnd": 4
              },
              "references": [
                {
                  "book": "Colossians",
                  "bookId": "COL",
                  "chapter": 3,
                  "verseStart": 1,
                  "verseEnd": 4
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", "
            },
            {
              "type": "scripture",
              "displayText": "Matthew 6:33, 9:36, 22:37-40",
              "reference": {
                "book": "Matthew",
                "bookId": "MAT",
                "chapter": 6,
                "verseStart": 33
              },
              "references": [
                {
                  "book": "Matthew",
                  "bookId": "MAT",
                  "chapter": 6,
                  "verseStart": 33
                },
                {
                  "book": "Matthew",
                  "bookId": "MAT",
                  "chapter": 9,
                  "verseStart": 36
                },
                {
                  "book": "Matthew",
                  "bookId": "MAT",
                  "chapter": 22,
                  "verseStart": 37,
                  "verseEnd": 40
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " When God brings alignment to our vision, it naturally overflows into mission. We fix our eyes on things above while putting our hands and feet to work for the people around us. What moves your heart? What needs or people stir something in you? Why is it important to seek God first before deciding what to pursue? How does consulting Him keep our vision aligned with His?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "q-share-it-2",
          "order": 2,
          "segments": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "After reading "
            },
            {
              "type": "scripture",
              "displayText": "1 Corinthians 13",
              "reference": {
                "book": "1 Corinthians",
                "bookId": "1CO",
                "chapter": 13
              },
              "references": [
                {
                  "book": "1 Corinthians",
                  "bookId": "1CO",
                  "chapter": 13
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", what do you notice about the difference between being aligned with love and simply doing the right Christian things? How should what you've noticed shape the way you live out your faith?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sec-self-reflection",
      "title": "SELF REFLECTION",
      "order": 4,
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "q-self-reflection-1",
          "order": 1,
          "segments": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "What feels out of alignment in my life right now? What would it look like to realign it with God in a healthy way?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "q-self-reflection-2",
          "order": 2,
          "segments": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Application is a key part of spiritual growth. Finish this sentence and carry it with you throughout the week:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "q-self-reflection-3",
          "order": 3,
          "segments": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "This week, I am aligning ____________________ with God's vision."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sec-guided-prayer",
      "title": "GUIDED PRAYER",
      "order": 5,
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "q-guided-prayer-1",
          "order": 1,
          "segments": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Jesus, break my heart for what breaks Yours. As You piece it back together, align my heart with Your love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness, and self-control. Help me see others the way You do. Grow my capacity to love as You love. And as You align our Crew together this fall, help us serve Your people in tangible ways. In Jesus' name, amen."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
